<Docs title="Troubleshooting"><div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">OPERATE / RECOVER</span><h1>Diagnose the boundary.</h1><p>A deny is normal. A transport, policy, audit, or shared-store failure must stop tool execution.</p></div><h2>Fast checks</h2><p>Check <code>/healthz</code>, <code>/readyz</code>, server logs, Kubernetes events, and the audit append error. Confirm policy and secret file permissions.</p><div class="docs-table"><div><b>401/403</b><span>Verify auth mode, issuer, callback, credentials, and Cedar inputs separately.</span></div><div><b>Policy unchanged</b><span>Invalid edits keep the last known-good snapshot; embedded authorizers must be rebuilt.</span></div><div><b>Audit failure</b><span>Stop tools and preserve evidence before checking disk, ownership, locking, and the chain sidecar.</span></div><div><b>Console state</b><span>Production sessions and rate limits require Redis-compatible shared stores and fail closed when unavailable.</span></div></div><p>See the complete <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/docs/troubleshooting.md">troubleshooting guide ↗</a>.</Docs>
